<title>FRANCE: Paris April '97 export traffic up 2.3 pct - ADP.</title>
<headline>Paris April '97 export traffic up 2.3 pct - ADP.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>April 1997 export traffic to the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 47,718 tonnes, an increase of 2.3 percent on the same period last year, Aeroports de Paris (ADP), figures show.</p>
<p>The Paris airports April 1997 import traffic, in tonnes, by region, with percentage change on April 1996, was:</p>
<p>    Domestic		 3,453  down  9.1</p>
<p>    European Union	 5,742  down  0.5</p>
<p>    Non-EU Europe	  1,322    up 21.1</p>
<p>    North Africa	     948    up 11.0</p>
<p>    Sub-Saharan Africa   3,687  down  5.2</p>
<p>    North America	 13,337    up  8.5</p>
<p>    French territories   2,296    up 13.9</p>
<p>    Latin America	  2,562  down  3.1</p>
<p>    Middle East	    4,798    up  0.7</p>
<p>    Far East		 9,573    up  0.3</p>
<p>    Total		   47,718    up  2.3</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
</text>
